# Vulnerabilities govulncheck reports against gwlint that cannot be fixed by
# upgrading, one ID per line. `mise run vulncheck` fails on anything reported
# that is not listed here, and also fails on an entry here that is no longer
# reported, so this file cannot quietly rot.
#
# Everything below reaches gwlint only through the package init() of code
# linked in transitively by kube-linter's lintcontext (helm, and containerd
# under helm). gwlint does not verify signatures and does not talk to a
# container runtime, so none of these sit on a path gwlint's own code drives.
# Re-check each on every kube-linter or helm upgrade.

# golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp is unmaintained and unsafe by design. Reached via
# helm's provenance verification, which gwlint never invokes. No fix exists;
# the package is deprecated outright.
GO-2026-5932

# containerd CRI checkpoint restore: CDI annotation smuggling. No fixed version
# published. gwlint never runs a CRI checkpoint restore.
GO-2026-5064

# containerd CRI checkpoint import: local image tag poisoning. No fixed version
# published. gwlint never imports a checkpoint.
GO-2026-5338

# containerd CRI checkpoint restore: arbitrary host CRI log file read via
# symlink following. No fixed version published. Same reachability as above.
GO-2026-5622
